        <p class="meta">2024 &middot; California State Capitol</p>
        <h3>SB 897: Making District of Choice Permanent</h3>
        <p>
          In 2024, I testified before the California Senate and Assembly Education Committees on SB 897, the bill that made California's District of Choice program permanent, working alongside Senator Josh Newman and advocates from more than fifteen school districts statewide.
        </p>
        <p style="color: rgba(244,239,225,0.65); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 10px;">
          District of Choice is the program that let me attend Walnut Valley schools instead of the district I would have been assigned to by default. I'd already lived what the bill was arguing for, so testifying for other students to have the same option felt like a tremendous honor and responsibility.
        </p>
        <a href="https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billNavClient.xhtml?bill_id=202320240SB897" class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="margin-top: 20px;">
